  "2026-09-28T06:20:10.124Z",claude-hub,"2026-09-28: pinned pm-ops 2026.9.28 and re-copied its templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts (pm-ops#124: the omit-dev skip now checks every Node resolution path for an incomplete hoisted pm-ops, so a broken ancestor install fails instead of silently skipping the merge drivers). release:check and changelog:check pass on this branch."
  "2026-10-02T22:10:28.268Z",codex-sol,"Restart by codex-sol: preserved remote PR #103 and all existing bot replies/reactions were inspected. Branch is already current with origin/main. No new actionable unresolved inline finding is present. Retain documented coverage/health/publication blockers; rerun unchanged full CI gate with the host-wide flock. No merge, publish or item closure."
  "2026-10-02T22:36:28.489Z",codex-sol,"Restart: reproduced CI exact project-local npm:pm-github@2026.9.26 installation and verified package version; restored the tracked managed registry exactly as CI does. Locked npm ci and unchanged release:check pass 280/280 tests, zero skips, measured index.ts 97.87% lines / 93.33% branches / 98.46% functions; statements are not separately reported. Canonical-reader, production audit, packed npm/Bun current/minimum host acceptance, changelog/date/attestation gates pass. The linked prepare suite initially refused foreign-ref trust; acknowledged authorized commands and reran successfully. Published canonical-template identity continues to cover ancestor-install handling. Coverage pm-todos-p60g and fail-closed pre-push privacy prerequisites remain open; issue-sync workflow stays disabled. No merge, publish or close; release claim for orchestrator."
  "2026-10-02T22:48:37.309Z",codex-sol,"Valid CodeRabbit/Cubic tracking correction: the #124 link note was stale, not a current publication blocker. Updated only the current doc-link note to identify pinned published pm-ops 2026.9.28; preserved every dated comment/note/history line. Full gate at 309a379 passed 280/280 plus canonical reader and packed npm/Bun. Coverage and pre-push privacy blockers remain."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T08:17:04.004Z",codex,"2026-09-27: Published CLI/SDK 2026.9.27 and pm-github 2026.9.26 installed through the project-local CLI; strict health passes with stale-item advisories. The published pm-ops launcher byte-identity test failed before copying its 2026.9.26 template, then the focused child-checkout suite passed 7/7 including incomplete directory and dangling link. Following a valid CodeRabbit privacy finding on the sibling pm-jira candidate, the checked-in scheduled sync job now has an if: false guard in addition to GitHub disabled_manually. The separate pre-push privacy gate is still absent; sync must not be enabled."
  "2026-09-27T08:27:21.211Z",codex,"2026-09-27 final guarded candidate: npm run release:check exits 0 after sync job if: false and PM link updates. 280/280 source tests pass with zero skips; index.ts honestly measures 97.87% lines, 93.33% branches, and 98.46% functions, with no statement metric. Docstring gate documents 81/81 declarations; zero production npm audit findings. Packed npm-current and bun-current against CLI/SDK 2026.9.27 and npm-minimum and bun-minimum against 2026.8.20 each imported 1 and exported 2 real fixture rows. The separate coverage item pm-todos-p60g remains open; the checked-in and GitHub scheduled sync are inert pending a fail-closed pre-push privacy gate. Exact-head CI and bot review remain to be completed after push."
  "2026-09-27T08:35:54.168Z",codex,"2026-09-27 exact-head Greptile P1 is valid: an incomplete ancestor node_modules/pm-ops can be treated as omit-dev by the published pm-ops 2026.9.26 launcher. The canonical source issue ops-jzp5 in unmerged pm-ops #124 already scans ancestor resolution paths and tests a real hoisted incomplete install. Keep this consumer PR open until the reviewed source is published, update the pin and byte-identical template, rerun full release and packed npm/Bun acceptance, and request a fresh exact-head review. CodeRabbit reported no actionable issue, but Greptile check fails on this head."
